                    {
                        "sense_id": "3df7f737-08c6-3bb1-a5bf-9abd22c5383f",
                        "entry_id": "aa372c70-b343-3af3-8bb5-d522e307bda9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Producing satisfied happiness and well-being."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ba25cde1-bc06-4d69-b6af-f2630724e761",
                                "sense_id": "3df7f737-08c6-3bb1-a5bf-9abd22c5383f",
                                "text": "During the 1960s and 1970s, many communist leaderships sought to legitimate their rule increasingly through the eudaemonic mode; the various economic reforms in the USSR and Eastern Europe at the time constituted the major symbol of this."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "48b8af89-29c3-4759-9cd2-0e0da684bbc9",
                                "sense_id": "3df7f737-08c6-3bb1-a5bf-9abd22c5383f",
                                "text": "In 2013, Cole examined the influence of well-being instead. He focused on two types: hedonic, from pleasure and rewards, and eudaemonic, from having a purpose beyond self-gratification."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
